From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:35:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: samsung,s2mm005: describe sink-pdos

The S2MM005 firmware requests the source's first capability, 5 V, by
itself, but the host can have it request another one. Say that the
connector's sink-pdos list the fixed supplies the host may pick, and
show them in the example.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml  | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml
index 2318f2643f..f918fdecd1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/samsung,s2mm005.yaml
@@ -12,11 +12,12 @@ maintainers:
 description:
   The S2MM005 is a USB Type-C port controller with a USB Power Delivery
   policy engine running in its own firmware, controlled over I2C. As a sink
-  it negotiates a power contract with the source by itself; the host reads
-  the attach state and the contract. As a source it relies on the VBUS
-  supply of the connector, and as a dual role data port on a USB role
-  switch connected to the connector's high speed port. It raises its
-  open-drain interrupt line while an event is pending.
+  it negotiates a power contract with the source by itself, at 5 V; the host
+  reads the attach state and the contract, and can have it request another
+  fixed supply that the connector's sink-pdos allow. As a source it relies
+  on the VBUS supply of the connector, and as a dual role data port on a
+  USB role switch connected to the connector's high speed port. It raises
+  its open-drain interrupt line while an event is pending.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -43,6 +44,7 @@ additionalProperties: false
 examples:
   - |
     #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/usb/pd.h>
 
     i2c {
         #address-cells = <1>;
@@ -58,6 +60,9 @@ examples:
                 label = "USB-C";
                 power-role = "sink";
                 data-role = "device";
+                sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, 0)
+                             PDO_FIXED(9000, 1650, 0)>;
+                op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
             };
         };
     };
